1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
Embedded machines must behave predictably —
especially when something fails.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
GENESIS RT turns machine requirements into
native QNX software, then proves how it behaves
when things go wrong.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Everything starts from a readable contract:
sensors, actuators, safety limits,
state transitions.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:29,500
The tooling validates strictly — invalid
input is rejected, never guessed.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:41,000
One click generates the native QNX controller:
guard server, periodic controller, device
endpoint, telemetry, supervisor.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:51,500
Deterministic codegen — the same contract
always yields byte-identical sources.

7
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:03,000
The controller compiles clean and runs
natively on QNX 8.0: synchronous message
passing, process isolation, live telemetry.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Sixteen on-target checks pass, and a thousand
performance samples are recorded for regression.

9
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:26,000
Now we break it on purpose. A seeded fault —
a stale proximity reading — is injected.

10
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:37,500
The guard denies the unsafe command and the
machine stops safe. Every run is reproducible
from its seed.

11
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:49,000
The failure becomes evidence. The twin replays
the exact trace, and the evidence graph links
the failed check to its requirement.

12
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Cause, not vibes.

13
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:12,000
Change one limit in the contract, and watch
behavior change on the target: the denied
probe is now allowed.

14
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:24,500
The limit check fails closed, exactly as
designed. Before and after, side by side,
from real campaigns.

15
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:34,000
The evidence passport seals the run:
hash-chained, replayable without our servers.

16
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:42,500
Modify one byte and replay rejects it.
Missing proof always fails closed.

17
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:55,000
GENESIS RT: from machine intent to verifiable
QNX behavior. Specify, compile, run, break,
prove — with evidence your whole team
can inspect.
